---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import './article.css';
import meta from './meta';

// Local images
import coverImg from './images/cover.svg';
import diagramImg from './images/diagram-architecture.svg';
import scoringImg from './images/feature-scoring.svg';
import timingImg from './images/feature-timing.svg';
import gridItem1 from './images/grid-item-1.svg';
import gridItem2 from './images/grid-item-2.svg';
import gridItem3 from './images/grid-item-3.svg';

// Reusable article components
import Callout from '../../components/article/Callout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/article/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<ArticleLayout meta={meta} wide={true}>
  <article class="article-template">

    <!-- Hero-specific content -->
    <p class="hero-lead">
      {meta.description}
    </p>

    <figure class="hero-cover">
      <img src={coverImg.src} alt="Article visual system showcase cover artwork" width="1200" height="560" loading="eager" />
      <figcaption>Figure — Architectural overview and pattern showcase for Coven of Technology editorial scrolls.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <!-- Mobile Table of Contents (visible on <= 980px) -->
    <details class="mobile-toc">
      <summary class="mobile-toc-summary">
        <span>☰ ON THIS SCROLL</span>
        <span style="font-size: 11px; opacity: 0.7;">EXPLORE</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="mobile-toc-content">
        <ul class="toc-nav-list" id="mobile-toc-list">
          <!-- Populated dynamically by client-side script from .article-section[data-toc-title] -->
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

    <div class="editorial-layout">

      <!-- Main content column -->
      <div class="main-content">

        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <!-- 01 · BASIC TYPOGRAPHY                                          -->
        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <section id="basic-typography" class="article-section" data-toc-title="Basic Typography">
          <div class="section-kicker">01 · BASIC TYPOGRAPHY</div>
          <h2>Editorial Headings & Typography System</h2>

          <!-- BLOCK: Title + Text -->
          <div class="block-typography-title-text">
            <div class="section-kicker">DEMO KICKER · SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE</div>
            <h3>Primary Section Heading Pattern</h3>
            <p>
              This example paragraph demonstrates a standard title and text block. In technical editorial writing, clear typographic hierarchy ensures the initiate absorbs complex doctrines with precision and ease.
            </p>
            <p>
              Placeholder text elaborating on the core architectural premise. Sentences are paced deliberately to cultivate a calm, authoritative editorial presence throughout the grimoire.
            </p>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Title + Text -->

          <!-- BLOCK: Text + Title -->
          <div class="block-typography-text-title">
            <p class="text-intro">
              Before introducing secondary subroutines, this introductory paragraph establishes operational context and transitions smoothly from the previous discussion into the following concept.
            </p>
            <h3 class="heading-subsequent">Subsequent Subsystem Heading</h3>
            <p>
              Following the transition, this body paragraph delivers the technical breakdown of the newly introduced mechanism, maintaining narrative continuity across editorial boundaries.
            </p>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Text + Title -->

          <!-- BLOCK: Solo Text -->
          <div class="block-solo-text">
            <p>
              This long editorial paragraph demonstrates comprehensive inline typography. Within this scroll, initiates can review <strong>bold emphases for critical tokens</strong>, <em>italicized passages denoting sacred axioms</em>, and inline hyperlinks directing the scholar to <a href="/library">The Grimoire Archive</a> or external documentation sources.
            </p>
            <p>
              Every line adheres to strict baseline rhythms and carefully tuned contrast ratios, ensuring legibility against the dark cosmic canvas even during protracted midnight research sessions.
            </p>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Solo Text -->
        </section>

        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <!-- 02 · LISTS & STEPS                                             -->
        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <section id="lists-and-steps" class="article-section" data-toc-title="Lists & Steps">
          <div class="section-kicker">02 · LISTS & STEPS</div>
          <h2>Lists, Inscriptions & Ordered Rituals</h2>

          <!-- BLOCK: Bullet List -->
          <div class="block-bullet-list">
            <h3 class="list-title">Core Archetype Principles</h3>
            <ul class="bullets-list">
              <li><strong>Deterministic Scoring:</strong> Propensity matrices calibrated against 90-day rolling interaction windows.</li>
              <li><strong>Audience Saturation Wards:</strong> Frequency caps preventing contact fatigue before unsubscribe events occur.</li>
              <li><strong>Temporal Synchronization:</strong> Message dispatch windows aligned with local subscriber engagement peaks.</li>
              <li><strong>Multi-Channel Telemetry:</strong> Seamless signal aggregation across Email, MobilePush, and CloudPages.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Bullet List -->

          <!-- BLOCK: Numbered Steps -->
          <div class="block-numbered-steps">
            <h3 class="list-title">Implementation Ritual Steps</h3>
            <ol class="steps-list">
              <li class="step-item">
                <div class="step-badge">01</div>
                <div class="step-content">
                  <h4>Telemetry Verification</h4>
                  <p>Verify that your business unit has captured a minimum threshold of 50,000 interactions over the preceding 90-day evaluation horizon.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="step-item">
                <div class="step-badge">02</div>
                <div class="step-content">
                  <h4>Feature Activation</h4>
                  <p>Navigate to Setup &gt; Einstein &gt; Engagement Scoring and toggle the activation rune to initiate model calibration.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="step-item">
                <div class="step-badge">03</div>
                <div class="step-content">
                  <h4>Model Training Horizon</h4>
                  <p>Allow 48 to 72 hours for the predictive engine to calculate initial propensity deciles and populate system data extensions.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="step-item">
                <div class="step-badge">04</div>
                <div class="step-content">
                  <h4>Journey Builder Deployment</h4>
                  <p>Insert Einstein Split activities into active journeys to steer contacts dynamically according to persona classifications.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Numbered Steps -->
        </section>

        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <!-- 03 · COLUMN LAYOUTS                                            -->
        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <section id="column-layouts" class="article-section" data-toc-title="Column Layouts">
          <div class="section-kicker">03 · COLUMN LAYOUTS</div>
          <h2>Modular Multi-Column Layouts</h2>

          <!-- BLOCK: Text | Image -->
          <div class="layout-text-media">
            <div class="layout-copy">
              <h3>Quadrant Propensity Matrix</h3>
              <p>
                This example demonstrates a 50/50 desktop layout with copy on the left and supporting visual media on the right. On tablet and mobile viewports, the layout gracefully stacks with copy preceding the illustration.
              </p>
              <p>
                Subscribers are categorized into four distinct quadrants based on predicted open and click probabilities, guiding personalized messaging cadence.
              </p>
            </div>
            <figure class="layout-media">
              <img src={scoringImg.src} alt="Quadrant Propensity Matrix demonstration" width="600" height="420" loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>Figure — Behavioral quadrant distribution across active contact base.</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Text | Image -->

          <!-- BLOCK: Image | Text -->
          <div class="layout-media-text">
            <figure class="layout-media">
              <img src={timingImg.src} alt="Temporal send time optimization distribution" width="600" height="420" loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>Figure — 168-hour probability matrix modeled per individual subscriber.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <div class="layout-copy">
              <h3>Temporal Distribution Curves</h3>
              <p>
                This pattern places media on the left and technical narrative on the right. Rather than resorting to direction inversions, semantic DOM ordering ensures accessibility and flawless responsive stacking.
              </p>
              <p>
                Send Time Optimization calculates individual response probability curves over a 168-hour weekly cycle, maximizing open engagement without batch congestion.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Image | Text -->

          <!-- BLOCK: Two Text Columns -->
          <div class="layout-2col">
            <div class="col-box">
              <h3>Inbound Channel Architecture</h3>
              <p>
                Demonstrating a balanced two-column text layout. Column A focuses on inbound engagement streams, telemetry ingestion, and webhook listeners that register subscriber actions in real-time.
              </p>
              <ul class="col-list">
                <li>API-triggered transactional events</li>
                <li>Real-time behavioral web events</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-box">
              <h3>Outbound Orchestration Pipeline</h3>
              <p>
                Column B addresses outbound dispatch engines, delivery queue priority, and automatic throttle policies that keep send volume safely within ISP thresholds.
              </p>
              <ul class="col-list">
                <li>Dynamic journey split routing</li>
                <li>Predictive quiet-hour suppression</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Two Text Columns -->

          <!-- BLOCK: Three Columns -->
          <div class="layout-3col">
            <div class="col-box">
              <div class="col-kicker">PILLAR I</div>
              <h3>Telemetry Ingestion</h3>
              <p>Captures continuous subscriber behavioral streams, normalizing raw click timestamps and interaction counters across enterprise units.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-box">
              <div class="col-kicker">PILLAR II</div>
              <h3>Predictive Modeling</h3>
              <p>Executes weekly machine learning training cycles, refreshing persona deciles and fatigue coefficients for every active subscriber.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-box">
              <div class="col-kicker">PILLAR III</div>
              <h3>Journey Activation</h3>
              <p>Translates model scores into deterministic splits, empowering automated journeys to adapt dispatch timing and content dynamically.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Three Columns -->
        </section>

        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <!-- 04 · IMAGES & MEDIA                                            -->
        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <section id="images-and-media" class="article-section" data-toc-title="Images & Media">
          <div class="section-kicker">04 · IMAGES & MEDIA</div>
          <h2>Visual Assets, Diagrams & Galleries</h2>

          <!-- BLOCK: Single Image -->
          <figure class="figure-single">
            <img src={coverImg.src} alt="Standard single figure diagram" width="1000" height="480" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Figure — Standard contained figure with subtle border and stylized caption.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Single Image -->

          <!-- BLOCK: Full Width Image -->
          <figure class="figure-full">
            <img src={diagramImg.src} alt="Full width architecture diagram" width="1200" height="600" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Figure — Full-width technical diagram spanning the entire width of the editorial column.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Full Width Image -->

          <!-- BLOCK: Two Images Grid -->
          <div class="image-grid-2">
            <figure class="figure-item">
              <img src={gridItem1.src} alt="Artifact classification asset" width="600" height="380" loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>Artifact 01 — Asset clustering and classification model.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="figure-item">
              <img src={gridItem2.src} alt="Audience fatigue saturation curve" width="600" height="380" loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>Artifact 02 — Audience fatigue saturation threshold curve.</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Two Images Grid -->

          <!-- BLOCK: Three Images Grid -->
          <div class="image-grid-3">
            <figure class="figure-item">
              <img src={gridItem1.src} alt="Visual feature classification" width="600" height="380" loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>Matrix A — Visual feature clustering</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="figure-item">
              <img src={gridItem2.src} alt="Fatigue threshold analysis" width="600" height="380" loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>Matrix B — Fatigue threshold analysis</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="figure-item">
              <img src={gridItem3.src} alt="NLP subject line prediction" width="600" height="380" loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>Matrix C — NLP subject prediction</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Three Images Grid -->

          <!-- BLOCK: Horizontal Gallery Scroll -->
          <div class="horizontal-scroll-wrap">
            <div class="horizontal-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Horizontal image gallery" tabindex="0">
              <figure class="gallery-card">
                <img src={gridItem1.src} alt="Gallery item 1 - Propensity Matrix" width="360" height="230" loading="lazy" />
                <figcaption>01 · Propensity Matrix Overview</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <figure class="gallery-card">
                <img src={gridItem2.src} alt="Gallery item 2 - Saturation Curve" width="360" height="230" loading="lazy" />
                <figcaption>02 · Saturation Decay Curve</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <figure class="gallery-card">
                <img src={gridItem3.src} alt="Gallery item 3 - Frequency Model" width="360" height="230" loading="lazy" />
                <figcaption>03 · Frequency Threshold Model</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <figure class="gallery-card">
                <img src={coverImg.src} alt="Gallery item 4 - Holistic Pipeline" width="360" height="230" loading="lazy" />
                <figcaption>04 · Holistic Pipeline Topology</figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>
            <div class="gallery-scroll-hint">✦ Scroll horizontally to inspect model artifacts</div>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Horizontal Gallery Scroll -->
        </section>

        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <!-- 05 · CARDS & COMPARISONS                                       -->
        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <section id="cards-and-comparisons" class="article-section" data-toc-title="Cards & Comparisons">
          <div class="section-kicker">05 · CARDS & COMPARISONS</div>
          <h2>Cards, Comparisons & Statistical Metrics</h2>

          <!-- BLOCK: 2-Card Grid -->
          <div class="card-grid-2">
            <div class="pattern-card">
              <div class="pattern-card-icon">✧</div>
              <h3 class="pattern-card-title">Supervised Propensity Models</h3>
              <p class="pattern-card-desc">Trained on historical engagement outcomes to classify subscribers into high, medium, and low likelihood deciles.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pattern-card">
              <div class="pattern-card-icon">◈</div>
              <h3 class="pattern-card-title">Unsupervised Cluster Models</h3>
              <p class="pattern-card-desc">Detects emergent subscriber behavioral groupings without pre-labeled categories to reveal hidden segment affinity.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: 2-Card Grid -->

          <!-- BLOCK: 3-Card Grid -->
          <div class="card-grid-3">
            <div class="pattern-card">
              <div class="pattern-card-icon">✉</div>
              <h3 class="pattern-card-title">Asset Propensity</h3>
              <p class="pattern-card-desc">Evaluates image tags, color palettes, and CTA phrasing to forecast message engagement prior to dispatch.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pattern-card">
              <div class="pattern-card-icon">⚙</div>
              <h3 class="pattern-card-title">Fatigue Horizons</h3>
              <p class="pattern-card-desc">Tracks saturation thresholds, redirecting recipients to passive holding paths when send density exceeds safety.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pattern-card">
              <div class="pattern-card-icon">✦</div>
              <h3 class="pattern-card-title">Lexical Predictor</h3>
              <p class="pattern-card-desc">Applies natural language analysis to subject lines to detect fatigue-inducing patterns and improve open rates.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: 3-Card Grid -->

          <!-- BLOCK: 50/50 Comparison -->
          <div class="comparison-split">
            <div class="comparison-column">
              <div class="comparison-col-header">
                <span class="comparison-col-icon">✉</span>
                <span>EMAIL STUDIO SIGNALS</span>
              </div>
              <ul class="comparison-list">
                <li>Unique and cumulative open timestamps</li>
                <li>Explicit click tracking and link category affinity</li>
                <li>Spam complaint rates and domain bounce thresholds</li>
                <li>Fatigue decay based on weekly broadcast density</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="comparison-column">
              <div class="comparison-col-header">
                <span class="comparison-col-icon">◈</span>
                <span>MOBILEPUSH SIGNALS</span>
              </div>
              <ul class="comparison-list">
                <li>Direct application opens from push banners</li>
                <li>In-app session duration following notification</li>
                <li>Quiet hour suppression per subscriber timezone</li>
                <li>Operating system notification permission state</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: 50/50 Comparison -->

          <!-- BLOCK: Stats & Metrics -->
          <div class="stats-grid">
            <div class="stat-card">
              <div class="stat-number">12</div>
              <div class="stat-label">Active Journeys</div>
              <div class="stat-sub">Multi-cloud orchestration</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-card">
              <div class="stat-number">89%</div>
              <div class="stat-label">Engagement Rate</div>
              <div class="stat-sub">Model-guided optimization</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-card">
              <div class="stat-number">42K</div>
              <div class="stat-label">Contacts Scored</div>
              <div class="stat-sub">90-day rolling window</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Stats & Metrics -->
        </section>

        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <!-- 06 · TABLES                                                    -->
        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <section id="tables" class="article-section" data-toc-title="Technical Tables">
          <div class="section-kicker">06 · TABLES</div>
          <h2>Responsive Technical Data Matrices</h2>
          <p>
            Technical articles frequently demand comparative data specifications. Below is an example of a responsive table that preserves internal horizontal scrollability on narrow viewports:
          </p>

          <!-- BLOCK: Responsive Technical Table -->
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table class="coven-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Predictive Feature</th>
                  <th>Email Studio</th>
                  <th>MobilePush</th>
                  <th>CloudPages / Web</th>
                  <th>Model Refresh Cycle</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Engagement Scoring</strong></td>
                  <td><span class="table-status status-active">Available</span></td>
                  <td><span class="table-status status-active">Available</span></td>
                  <td><span class="table-status status-beta">Beta</span></td>
                  <td>Weekly (Sunday UTC)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Send Time Optimization</strong></td>
                  <td><span class="table-status status-active">Available</span></td>
                  <td><span class="table-status status-active">Available</span></td>
                  <td><span class="table-status status-disabled">N/A</span></td>
                  <td>Continuous (168-hr matrix)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Engagement Frequency</strong></td>
                  <td><span class="table-status status-active">Available</span></td>
                  <td><span class="table-status status-beta">Beta</span></td>
                  <td><span class="table-status status-disabled">N/A</span></td>
                  <td>Daily aggregation</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Content Selection</strong></td>
                  <td><span class="table-status status-active">Available</span></td>
                  <td><span class="table-status status-disabled">N/A</span></td>
                  <td><span class="table-status status-active">Available</span></td>
                  <td>Real-time per dispatch</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Responsive Technical Table -->
        </section>

        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <!-- 07 · CALLOUTS & QUOTES                                         -->
        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <section id="callouts-and-quotes" class="article-section" data-toc-title="Callouts & Quotes">
          <div class="section-kicker">07 · CALLOUTS & QUOTES</div>
          <h2>Callouts, Advisories & Editorial Quotes</h2>

          <!-- BLOCK: Callouts (Info, Warning, Tip, Note) -->
          <div class="block-callouts-group">
            <Callout type="info" title="Arcane Telemetry Note">
              <p>
                Einstein requires a minimum threshold of <strong>50,000 interactions</strong> across your business unit over the preceding 90 days. Below this threshold, predictions fallback to organic average metrics.
              </p>
            </Callout>

            <Callout type="warning" title="Ward of Caution">
              <p>
                Never place an Einstein STO activity directly after a Wait Activity with a fixed hour; the two timers will conflict and cause asynchronous queuing delays in the contact journey.
              </p>
            </Callout>

            <Callout type="tip" title="Craft Mastery Tip">
              <p>
                Query the <code>_Einstein_MC_Predictive_Scores</code> system data extension via Automation Studio SQL to export raw propensity deciles into your external data lake.
              </p>
            </Callout>

            <Callout type="note" title="Grimoire Reference">
              <p>
                Refer to Salesforce Trailhead module <em>Einstein for Marketing Cloud: Quick Look</em> for setup prerequisites and permissions.
              </p>
            </Callout>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Callouts (Info, Warning, Tip, Note) -->

          <!-- BLOCK: Pullquote -->
          <div class="pullquote">
            <p class="pullquote-text">
              "A predictive algorithm that operates without architectural intent is merely noise cast into the dark. Master the signal, and every dispatch finds its rightful mark."
            </p>
            <span class="pullquote-author">— Coven Principle of Predictive Divination</span>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Pullquote -->
        </section>

        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <!-- 08 · CODE INSCRIPTIONS                                         -->
        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <section id="code" class="article-section" data-toc-title="Code Inscriptions">
          <div class="section-kicker">08 · CODE</div>
          <h2>Syntax-Highlighted Code Inscriptions</h2>
          <p>
            When coordinating cross-cloud journeys between Salesforce Core and Marketing Cloud, use a deterministic handler to consume Einstein segment classifications:
          </p>

          <!-- BLOCK: Code Block -->
          <CodeBlock title="EinsteinSyncHandler.cls" language="apex">
{`// Sacred Controller: Synchronizing Einstein Persona to Salesforce Core
public with sharing class EinsteinSyncHandler {
    @InvocableMethod(label='Sync Einstein Persona' description='Updates contact record with AI Persona')
    public static void updatePersonas(List<Id> contactIds) {
        List<Contact> recordsToUpdate = new List<Contact>();
        for (Contact c : [SELECT Id, Einstein_Persona__c FROM Contact WHERE Id IN :contactIds]) {
            // Re-align loyalty tier based on predicted score and trigger asynchronous enterprise telemetry pipeline invocation across multi-cloud boundaries
            if (c.Einstein_Persona__c == 'Loyalist') {
                c.Tier__c = 'VIP Archmage';
                recordsToUpdate.add(c);
            }
        }
        if (!recordsToUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update recordsToUpdate;
        }
    }
}`}
          </CodeBlock>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Code Block -->
        </section>

        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <!-- 09 · INTERACTIVE BLOCKS                                        -->
        <!-- ============================================================== -->
        <section id="interaction" class="article-section" data-toc-title="Interactive Blocks">
          <div class="section-kicker">09 · INTERACTION</div>
          <h2>Interactive FAQ & Use Case Exercises</h2>

          <!-- BLOCK: FAQ Accordion -->
          <div class="faq-list">
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>How long does it take for models to initialize after activation?</summary>
              <div class="faq-body">
                <p>
                  Initial model training requires up to <strong>72 hours</strong> once the prerequisite 50,000 subscriber interactions have been ingested. Subsequent re-training occurs on a weekly cadence automatically.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>Does Apple Mail Privacy Protection (MPP) skew open scores?</summary>
              <div class="faq-body">
                <p>
                  Salesforce has integrated MPP filtering algorithms that de-weight automated proxy cache pre-fetches, focusing on confirmed intent signals like click timestamps and zero-party interactions.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>Can Einstein scores be extracted using Automation Studio SQL?</summary>
              <div class="faq-body">
                <p>
                  Yes. By querying the Einstein Data Extensions provisioned in your enterprise account (e.g. <code>_Einstein_MC_Predictive_Scores</code>), you can join scores with custom master subscriber tables.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: FAQ Accordion -->

          <!-- BLOCK: Exercises with Reveal Answer -->
          <div class="exercise-group">
            <div class="exercise-card">
              <span class="exercise-badge">TRIAL SCENARIO 01</span>
              <p class="exercise-scenario">
                <strong>Scenario:</strong> A retail enterprise notices that 38% of their subscriber base opens emails faithfully every Friday afternoon, but click rates have dropped by half due to promotional saturation. Which Einstein feature should be configured first?
              </p>
              <button type="button" class="reveal-btn" aria-expanded="false" data-target="ans-1">
                <span>✦ Reveal Answer</span>
              </button>
              <div id="ans-1" class="reveal-answer">
                <strong>Solution: Einstein Engagement Frequency.</strong>
                <p>The subscribers are "Window Shoppers" suffering from saturation. Capping the frequency prevents fatigue while dynamic content testing within the existing send window restores click engagement.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="exercise-card">
              <span class="exercise-badge">TRIAL SCENARIO 02</span>
              <p class="exercise-scenario">
                <strong>Scenario:</strong> A global conference announcement must reach attendees across 14 timezones simultaneously on Tuesday without sending during the middle of the night. Which node should be placed in Journey Builder?
              </p>
              <button type="button" class="reveal-btn" aria-expanded="false" data-target="ans-2">
                <span>✦ Reveal Answer</span>
              </button>
              <div id="ans-2" class="reveal-answer">
                <strong>Solution: Einstein Send Time Optimization (STO) with a 24-Hour Send Window.</strong>
                <p>The 24-hour window allows Einstein to calculate the recipient's local timezone probability, ensuring arrival during wakeful hours without manual timezone splitting.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- END BLOCK: Exercises with Reveal Answer -->
        </section>

